@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Daily Grind partial updates
+
+`npm run build` checks the polyfill JavaScript and copies the static site to
+`dist/`, preserving processing instructions verbatim. No server is needed to build.
+
+The final template in `index.html` can be streamed after the page shell. It replaces
+the loading state inside `seasonal-favorites-content`. The persistent heading and
+polite live region label and announce updates. Cards reserve their initial height;
+without JavaScript or native patching, the original menu is available via `noscript`.
+
+Later server payloads can target `seasonal-favorites`, `maple-oat-latte`,
+`dark-roast-espresso`, or `cold-brew`. Each replacement must include its own
+`<?start name="…">` / `<?end>` range again to allow repeated updates. A whole-section
+replacement should also retain the card IDs and their ranges.
+
+For example, append this after the initial template in the same HTML response:
+
+```html
+<template for="cold-brew">
+  <?start name="cold-brew">
+  <h3>Cold Brew</h3>
+  <p>Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness.</p>
+  <a href="/menu/cold-brew" class="btn">View Details</a>
+  <?end>
+</template>
+```
+
+After the deferred polyfills have loaded (`DOMContentLoaded`), JavaScript can use
+the native setters directly on the persistent section or card containers:
+
+```js
+const card = document.getElementById('cold-brew');
+if (!(card instanceof HTMLElement)) throw new Error('Cold Brew card is unavailable');
+
+// Application-controlled HTML only. Retain the range for later declarative patches.
+card.setHTMLUnsafe(`<?start name="cold-brew">
+  <h3>Cold Brew</h3>
+  <p>Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness.</p>
+  <a href="/menu/cold-brew" class="btn">View Details</a>
+<?end>`);
+
+// A trusted endpoint may instead supply the same marked-up card content in chunks.
+// This endpoint is illustrative; the static site does not provide an API.
+const response = await fetch('/api/seasonal/cold-brew');
+if (!response.ok || !response.body) throw new Error('Seasonal update failed');
+await response.body.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()).pipeTo(card.streamHTMLUnsafe());
+```
+
+Use `seasonal-favorites-content` for whole-section setters (the grid and card ranges
+belong inside its content). These unsafe setters preserve processing instructions;
+use them only for trusted application markup, with script execution left disabled.
+For untrusted content, use a supported safe `setHTML()` / `streamHTML()` sanitizer
+instead, and do not rely on it preserving patch markers. Under enforced Trusted
+Types, provide the application's approved `TrustedHTML` rather than a plain string.
+
+Avoid replacing content containing keyboard focus; defer such updates until focus
+leaves the affected container. Background updates should not move focus.
+
+The local Apache-2.0 polyfills are pinned to version 0.1.1 from
+[html-setters-polyfill](https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/html-setters-polyfill) and
+[template-for-polyfill](https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/template-for-polyfill).
+The template fallback uses mutation observers; the setters fallback buffers streams
+until close and requires native `setHTML` for safe setters. Supporting browsers use
+native streaming. The local copies avoid a runtime CDN dependency.
